// What every fixture's tsconfig had written out in full, seventy-three times.
//
// A fixture is a tiny app the analyzer is pointed at, so its config is the same config every time —
// only what it POINTS AT differs. Two things stay in the child, and neither is a style choice:
//
// - `include`, because a relative path in it resolves against the config that DECLARES it. `"."` here
//   would mean all of `fixtures/`, so every fixture would pull in every other one.
// - `paths`, for the same reason: TypeScript records a `pathsBasePath` per config file, so a mapping
//   written here would resolve against `fixtures/` rather than against the fixture that needs it.
//
// `jsxImportSource` is safe to share because it is a module specifier resolved from each SOURCE FILE,
// not from the config — `..` is `fixtures/jsx-runtime.ts` from any fixture, at any depth of one.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ESNext",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "jsxImportSource": "..",
    "strict": false,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  }
}
